{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "f9c8a91f8d7eb7a3",
			"type": "group",
			"x": -50,
			"y": -425,
			"width": 1680,
			"height": 850,
			"label": "Chapter 1 Part 1"
		},
		{
			"id": "aa421056a21a88e3",
			"type": "group",
			"x": 4570,
			"y": 95,
			"width": 3360,
			"height": 670,
			"label": "Chapter 3"
		},
		{
			"id": "7fd7c9cd9977d361",
			"type": "group",
			"x": 2470,
			"y": -425,
			"width": 1260,
			"height": 850,
			"label": "Chapter 2 Part 1"
		},
		{
			"id": "0c735c4ffef67d00",
			"type": "group",
			"x": 2470,
			"y": 495,
			"width": 1680,
			"height": 665,
			"label": "Chapter 2 Part 2"
		},
		{
			"id": "ee77a78553f5e8a7",
			"type": "group",
			"x": -50,
			"y": 495,
			"width": 1680,
			"height": 665,
			"label": "Chapter 1 Part 2"
		},
		{
			"id": "3ef5012836ca946f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Change the definition of intelligence",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2100,
			"y": 380,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "cca3f39d2e9856e2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Early Definition of Intelligence in AI\n- Capacity to optimize a given objective specified by its designers \n- Assumes an isomorphism between formal language and human meaning",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": -420,
			"y": 300,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 260
		},
		{
			"id": "3dcf784376b9ba31",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Formal representations of complex goals are not practical",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 810,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "8e3c9c15ae7b1439",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The standard model AI's conception of intelligence leads to inscrutable safety problems",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 1680,
			"y": -65,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "bc8a12b9f528f339",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Goals that are more abstract in nature require formal specification",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 0,
			"y": 795,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "dc58144d592038f5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Develop Expert Systems",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 420,
			"y": 825,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "6467fd24b1413bad",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Knowledge Acquisition Bottleneck\n- Systems were hard to maintain\n- Brittle\n- Didn't work well outside of their own *Context*",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 840,
			"y": 745,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 230
		},
		{
			"id": "0ea67c62f027dab9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "AI Winter 1987-1993",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 1260,
			"y": 825,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "deca3a75af59ba6a",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Goals that can be articulated discretely, as a numeric value, in a particular context really require tacit description in an objective context.\n- The amount of oil produced can be represented as the quantity of liquid accumulated by its sensors \n- But comes with the implication that you would rather have less oil than destroy the planet.",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 0,
			"y": -55,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 390
		},
		{
			"id": "53bc82ec5507dfb2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Anything that has a discrete representation can be optimized",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 0,
			"y": -200,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "7c4177895d37cb77",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "We have to instill the system with notions that carry tacit understanding such as: Values and Beliefs",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 420,
			"y": -375,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "1c7d86b3d083c8bf",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Orthogonality Thesis: 'Intelligence' can grow independent of values and beliefs",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 420,
			"y": -65,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "969ac3e41aafcfa9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Any System in an objective context with a goal would naturally desire harmful things",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 420,
			"y": 235,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "fa16698babbecac7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Docility: We need a system that will listen to us.",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 840,
			"y": 250,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "bf071a390e0a7e1e",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The Value Specification problem: We need to formally represent tacit concepts",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 840,
			"y": -365,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "25a01ded683c6956",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Standard Model of AI and of AI safety",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 1260,
			"y": -50,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "45c37b55dea49e32",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Argued by Stuart Russell",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2520,
			"y": -335,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "7019a368388834e5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Aggregate human preferences to represent this objective as a utility function",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2940,
			"y": -65,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "1d54d742a707cc32",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Change the goal from being a certain objective to an uncertain one.",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2520,
			"y": -65,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "7a6c45db5fbb20e6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Utility function, while containing more information about the goal, still runs into the Value Specification Problem",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3360,
			"y": -75,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "4368381ba3ffbf83",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Model off Human Behavior",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2520,
			"y": 265,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "f0f14cf3748c3ffa",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Solves Docility in principle as the model will listen to us",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2940,
			"y": 250,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "289fb1db1c86638f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Reintroduces the issue of Docility as there are still gaps in the model's understanding of our behavior",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3360,
			"y": 225,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "966e7101ee14f59d",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Create a representation of the difference between two pieces of data",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2940,
			"y": 795,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "9dfadbeb85c7d50d",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Loss Function",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3360,
			"y": 825,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "015ea8bb81113227",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Neural Networks / Other probabilistic models",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3360,
			"y": 1010,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "58720857911c52c4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Create a system that can learn this difference",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2940,
			"y": 1010,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 100
		},
		{
			"id": "1f078a5f5d489abf",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The model represents what the Data can represent, and how we label that data",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3360,
			"y": 595,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "3b04ecbccc442bbf",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Aggregate mass amounts of data",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2940,
			"y": 625,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "2749843c0b0ec15f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The problem of formal representation is pushed back but still holds in the necessity of these formalities",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 3780,
			"y": 785,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "e8d82d9ac0a583d3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Change the formal representation to be learned from the Data \n- The relation between the data itself carries more information than we can formally specify",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2520,
			"y": 800,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 200
		},
		{
			"id": "4527081eb872b391",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Both the Safety and Functionality of AI is Bottlenecked by the formal representations they boil down to, either in our specification or in the data",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 4620,
			"y": 340,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "69c94486a69a0d89",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Halevy, Norvig, and Pereira later gave this shift its slogan in “The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Data”",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 2520,
			"y": 545,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "d68cf97f84fd7c62",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Follow-the-data approaches can only work if the data is at bottom meaningful to us",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 5040,
			"y": 365,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "f71beff62b0d2b58",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Language is possibly the only type of data that has both a formal representation and is intrinsically meaningful to us.",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 5460,
			"y": 355,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "595fe62419d950ab",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Model Language",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 5880,
			"y": 395,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "b6ea6222afdb7151",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Aggregated data existed without the necessity to label it; it labels itself",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 6300,
			"y": 145,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "8ae37922fa6d563f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "The loss function as cross-entropy loss is not as arbitrary because the data is represented as intrinsically meaningful language. (Weak)",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 6300,
			"y": 340,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "4c2173f2c67e5145",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Transformer architecture is sufficiently flexible to model complex features of the corpus",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 6300,
			"y": 585,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 130
		},
		{
			"id": "894d3c5e69fdb170",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Modeling language is docile as it has an incentive to write like we write, and understanding how \"we\" write is not arbitrarily defined",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 6720,
			"y": 220,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "5b579570f727d5b7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Not all of how \"we\" write is desirable to model and not all the tacit knowledge we carry is desirable to represent",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 7140,
			"y": 355,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		},
		{
			"id": "c5d6c57e545ee68d",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "New Problem of Alignment",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 7560,
			"y": 395,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 70
		},
		{
			"id": "c220a315cb7f8039",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Modeling Language solves the Value Specification Problem as language carries this tacit knowledge",
			"styleAttributes": {},
			"x": 6720,
			"y": 475,
			"width": 320,
			"height": 150
		}
	],
